{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>Lest your heart be deceived.</b> From the root פתיות (folly/naïveté), like ופותה תמית קנאה — that is, <b>take heed for yourselves, lest your heart be deceived</b> and act foolishly. Had it been from the root of persuasion, it should have said פן יפותה, like יפותה קצין." "<b>And you serve other Elohim.</b> Rabbi Yossi says: why are they called by the name Elohim? So as not to give an opening to the inhabitants of the world to say, 'If they had been called by the same name as Him, there would be a need for them.' But they are called by His name, and there is no need for them." "<b>Others.</b> Because they are made 'others' — if it is of gold, and its owner needs something, he exchanges it and makes it something else, of silver; and if it was of silver, he makes it something else, of copper."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:52:27.766368106Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}